<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply unchanged in Aug 19 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply unchanged in Aug 19 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply was unchanged in the August 19 week at $3,764.6 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $400 million to $4,759.0 billion. M-1 fell $3.7 billion to $1,096.7 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,762.3 billion versus $3,759.4 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
